1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,000
Your DNA is wrapped
around histones.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,000
Small chemical marks on them decide
which genes are open and read,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,600
and which stay locked.

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,600
Every cell type reads
different genes.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,700
But most epigenome profiling blends
a whole tissue into one average.

6
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,000
NEXUS Epigenomics was founded in
Stockholm in 2024 to close that gap,

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,800
with ready-to-use kits built on methods
published in Nature Biotechnology.

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,900
What is your biggest gap?
